# I2P config + netDb — the router writes here via i2prouter (PID, logs, netDb,
# peerProfiles, etc.). Must be pre-created so a Docker named volume at this path
# is initialised with the correct ownership (B19_UID:B19_GID); otherwise Docker
# auto-creates the volume’s root as root:root and the wrapper fails with
# “Permission denied” on /app/.i2p/i2p.pid (reproduced with
# -v test-i2p-netdb:/app/.i2p). See b19/ubuntu docs/how-to/use-build.d.md#volume-directories.
${B19_HOME}/.i2p
# Eepsite identity key + cache — persisted separately in dev; kiota’s router
# mounts only .i2p (eepsite disabled there), but local dev needs this too.
${XDG_DATA_HOME}
${XDG_CACHE_HOME}/tmp
